#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:1
msgid "Release 1.9 (2015-06-12)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:3
msgid ""
"In addition to the usual bug fixes, this release has the following new "
"features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:6
msgid ""
"Signed binary cache support. You can enable signature checking by adding the "
"following to `nix.conf`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:12
msgid ""
"This will prevent Nix from downloading any binary from the cache that is not "
"signed by one of the keys listed in `binary-cache-public-keys`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:16
msgid ""
"Signature checking is only supported if you built Nix with the `libsodium` "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:19
msgid ""
"Note that while Nix has had experimental support for signed binary caches "
"since version 1.7, this release changes the signature format in a backwards-"
"incompatible way."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:23
msgid ""
"Automatic downloading of Nix expression tarballs. In various places, you can "
"now specify the URL of a tarball containing Nix expressions (such as "
"Nixpkgs), which will be downloaded and unpacked automatically. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:28
msgid "In `nix-env`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:30
msgid ""
"    $ nix-env -f https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-channels/archive/"
"nixos-14.12.tar.gz -iA firefox\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:32
msgid ""
"This installs Firefox from the latest tested and built revision of the NixOS "
"14.12 channel."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:35
msgid "In `nix-build` and `nix-shell`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:37
msgid ""
"    $ nix-build https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/archive/master.tar.gz -A "
"hello\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:39
msgid ""
"This builds GNU Hello from the latest revision of the Nixpkgs master branch."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:42
msgid ""
"In the Nix search path (as specified via `NIX_PATH` or `-I`). For example, "
"to start a shell containing the Pan package from a specific version of "
"Nixpkgs:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:46
msgid ""
"    $ nix-shell -p pan -I nixpkgs=https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-channels/"
"archive/8a3eea054838b55aca962c3fbde9c83c102b8bf2.tar.gz\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:48
msgid "In `nixos-rebuild` (on NixOS):"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:50
msgid ""
"    $ nixos-rebuild test -I nixpkgs=https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-"
"channels/archive/nixos-unstable.tar.gz\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:52
msgid "In Nix expressions, via the new builtin function `fetchTarball`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:54
msgid ""
"    with import (fetchTarball https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-channels/"
"archive/nixos-14.12.tar.gz) {}; …\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:56
msgid "(This is not allowed in restricted mode.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:58
msgid "`nix-shell` improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:60
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` now has a flag `--run` to execute a command in the `nix-shell` "
"environment, e.g. `nix-shell --run make`. This is like the existing `--"
"command` flag, except that it uses a non-interactive shell (ensuring that "
"hitting Ctrl-C won’t drop you into the child shell)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:66
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` can now be used as a `#!`\\-interpreter. This allows you to "
"write scripts that dynamically fetch their own dependencies. For example, "
"here is a Haskell script that, when invoked, first downloads GHC and the "
"Haskell packages on which it depends:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:72
msgid ""
"    #! /usr/bin/env nix-shell\n"
"    #! nix-shell -i runghc -p haskellPackages.ghc haskellPackages.HTTP\n"
"    \n"
"    import Network.HTTP\n"
"    \n"
"    main = do\n"
"      resp <- Network.HTTP.simpleHTTP (getRequest \"http://nixos.org/\")\n"
"      body <- getResponseBody resp\n"
"      print (take 100 body)\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:82
msgid ""
"Of course, the dependencies are cached in the Nix store, so the second "
"invocation of this script will be much faster."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:85
msgid "Chroot improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:87
msgid ""
"Chroot builds are now supported on Mac OS X (using its sandbox mechanism)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:90
msgid ""
"If chroots are enabled, they are now used for all derivations, including "
"fixed-output derivations (such as `fetchurl`). The latter do have network "
"access, but can no longer access the host filesystem. If you need the old "
"behaviour, you can set the option `build-use-chroot` to `relaxed`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:96
msgid ""
"On Linux, if chroots are enabled, builds are performed in a private PID "
"namespace once again. (This functionality was lost in Nix 1.8.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:100
msgid ""
"Store paths listed in `build-chroot-dirs` are now automatically expanded to "
"their closure. For instance, if you want `/nix/store/…-bash/bin/sh` mounted "
"in your chroot as `/bin/sh`, you only need to say `build-chroot-dirs "
"=                                                 /bin/sh=/nix/store/…-bash/"
"bin/sh`; it is no longer necessary to specify the dependencies of Bash."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:107
msgid ""
"The new derivation attribute `passAsFile` allows you to specify that the "
"contents of derivation attributes should be passed via files rather than "
"environment variables. This is useful if you need to pass very long strings "
"that exceed the size limit of the environment. The Nixpkgs function "
"`writeTextFile` uses this."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:113
msgid ""
"You can now use `~` in Nix file names to refer to your home directory, e.g. "
"`import         ~/.nixpkgs/config.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:117
msgid ""
"Nix has a new option `restrict-eval` that allows limiting what paths the Nix "
"evaluator has access to. By passing `--option restrict-eval true` to Nix, "
"the evaluator will throw an exception if an attempt is made to access any "
"file outside of the Nix search path. This is primarily intended for Hydra to "
"ensure that a Hydra jobset only refers to its declared inputs (and is "
"therefore reproducible)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:124
msgid ""
"`nix-env` now only creates a new “generation” symlink in `/nix/var/nix/"
"profiles` if something actually changed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:127
msgid ""
"The environment variable `NIX_PAGER` can now be set to override `PAGER`. You "
"can set it to `cat` to disable paging for Nix commands only."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:131
msgid "Failing `<...>` lookups now show position information."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:133
msgid ""
"Improved Boehm GC use: we disabled scanning for interior pointers, which "
"should reduce the “`Repeated         allocation of very large block`” "
"warnings and associated retention of memory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:138
msgid ""
